<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    DPS ladder rebalance, applied by ModAdjusterV2 (workshop 3017795356) as field-level patches.
    No SBC definitions are overridden. Gatling fire rate / reload changes live in Gatling.xml.

    RATIONALE
    Vanilla burst and reload values were set weapon by weapon, which produced odd results:
      - Fixed gatlings and autocannons never pause to reload, so they out-damaged their turrets by 30-55%.
      - Small turrets got longer reloads than large ones (gatling 6 s vs 4 s).
      - The assault cannon reloaded 6 s after every shot, so the small gun and small turret did less DPS
        than a gatling, breaking the "bigger caliber = more DPS" trend.
    Goals:
      1. Fixed guns and single-barrel turrets of a caliber do the same DPS.
      2. DPS rises steadily with caliber: gatling < autocannon < assault cannon < artillery.
      3. Keep Keen's design of double-barrel large turrets (assault cannon, artillery: burst of 2 per reload)
         doing roughly double the DPS of their single-barrel versions.
      4. Damage per round is unchanged here, so ammo cost per damage is unchanged.

    Effective rate of fire = burst / ((burst - 1) / RPM + reload).
    DPS vs large light armor (balance spreadsheet formula; cannons count full penetration pool + explosion):

    Caliber          Fixed            Large turret       Small turret      Change
    ===============  ===============  =================  ================  ==========================================
    Gatling          1,050 -> 803     792 -> 806         703 -> 806        Gatling.xml: fixed 900 RPM, small turret 4 s reload
    Autocannon       1,250 -> 1,000   800 -> 1,000       800 -> 1,000      Fixed 150 -> 120 RPM; turrets reload 4 -> 2 s
    Assault cannon   700 -> 1,200     1,326 -> 2,191     700 -> 1,200      Reload 6 -> 3.5 s on all three
    Artillery        1,458            2,745              (none)            Unchanged

    Fixed bullet weapons (gatling, autocannon) ignore reloads in practice, so their fire rate is lowered instead.
    JS - Weapon Overhaul's LargeAutocannonTurret weapon is patched by Data\Scripts\JS - Weapon Rebalance\OptionalModWeaponTuning.cs
    instead, because ModAdjusterV2 throws KeyNotFoundException on missing WeaponDefinitions when Overhaul is not loaded.
-->
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <Weapons>
        <!-- ===== Autocannon: 1,000 DPS ===== -->
        <!--
            Fixed small-grid autocannon: 120 RPM x 500 dmg = 1,000 DPS (one shot every 30 ticks).
            ModAdjuster only applies ProjectileAmmoData when AmmoMagazines is in the same entry, and rebuilds it,
            so the vanilla sound and burst are included.
        -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>Autocannon</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <ProjectileAmmoData RateOfFire="120" ShootSoundName="WepShipAutocannonShot" ShotsInBurst="16" />
            <AmmoMagazines>
                <AmmoMagazine Subtype="AutocannonClip" />
            </AmmoMagazines>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Small-grid autocannon turret (also the Warfare 3 Type II): 16 shots in 6 s, then 2 s reload = 120 RPM effective -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>AutocannonTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <ReloadTime>2000</ReloadTime>
        </Weapon>

        <!-- ===== Assault cannon: reload 6 -> 3.5 s ===== -->
        <!-- Fixed small-grid assault cannon (also the Warfare 3 Type II): 1 shot per 3.5 s = ~1,200 DPS -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>SmallMediumCalibreGun</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <ReloadTime>3500</ReloadTime>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Small-grid assault cannon turret (also the Warfare 3 Type II): 1 shot per 3.5 s = ~1,200 DPS -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>SmallMediumCalibreTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <ReloadTime>3500</ReloadTime>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Large-grid assault cannon turret (also the Warfare 3 Type II): 2 shots per 3.5 s = ~2,191 DPS (double barrel) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>MediumCalibreTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <ReloadTime>3500</ReloadTime>
        </Weapon>
    </Weapons>
</Definitions>
